---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site, isTodo } from '../data/site';

/**
 * Cost, shape of the year, how to visit before committing, what happens next.
 * The numbers are placeholders on purpose: fees change annually and vary by
 * council, and a wrong figure on this page is the one a family remembers.
 */
const registrationReady = !isTodo(site.registrationUrl);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Join"
  description="How to join Cub Scout Pack 662 in New York City: what it costs, what the year looks like, and how to visit before you decide."
>
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Join Pack 662</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        You're welcome to visit our pack to see if scouting is a fit for your cub and family!
      </p>

      <div class="icon-head">
        <Icon name="people" />
        <h2>Who can join</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Any child in kindergarten through fifth grade, and their family. You do not
        need any Scouting background, or camping experience!
      </p>
      <p class="meta">
        Older than that? Scouts BSA takes youth from about halfway through fifth
        grade, whether or not they were Cub Scouts. Two troops are hosted by the same
        church we are:{' '}
        {site.partnerTroops.map((t, i) => (
          <>
            {i > 0 && ' and '}
            <a href={t.url}>{t.name}</a> for {t.forWhom}
          </>
        ))}.
      </p>

      <div class="icon-head">
        <Icon name="star" />
        <h2>What it costs</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        There are two main charges: the national and council registration fee, and the pack dues. Uniforms and books are separate.
      </p>
      <dl class="facts">
        <dt>Scouting America registration</dt>
        <dd>
          <strong>{site.cost.registration}</strong> per Scout, covering national and
          council. Set for us, not by us, and it renews on the date you joined rather
          than in September.
        </dd>
        <dt>Pack dues</dt>
        <dd>
          <strong>{site.cost.dues}</strong> per Scout, running from September and
          invoiced through Scoutbook once your child is registered. Dues buy adventure
          loops and pins, snacks and supplies, advancement ceremonies, Pinewood and
          Regatta kits, leader training and the annual recharter.
        </dd>
        <dt>Joining partway through the year</dt>
        <dd>{site.cost.proration}</dd>
        <dt>Activity fees</dt>
        <dd>
          <strong>{site.cost.activityFees}</strong>, for council campouts and the extra
          Webelos and Arrow of Light trips. Most of these are optional.
        </dd>
        <dt>If cost is a barrier</dt>
        <dd>{site.cost.assistance}</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="meta">
        Uniform is separate; check the pack&rsquo;s uniform exchange before you buy
        anything.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">
        Uniform and handbook are separate. See <a href="/resources">Resources</a> for
        where to get them, and the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> for what you can put off
        buying.
      </p>

      <div class="icon-head">
        <Icon name="calendar" />
        <h2>What the year looks like</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Scouting year follows the school year. Dens meet through the fall and
        spring, the whole pack comes together less often, and there are outings and
        at least one campout mixed in. Our schedule is on the{' '}
        <a href="/meetings">meetings page</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="icon-head">
        <Icon name="tent" />
        <h2>Visit before you commit</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Come to a meeting and see whether your child likes it. Click below to email us, include your
        child's name & grade and we will tell you which meeting to come to and what den you're in!
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="cta" href={`mailto:${site.email.pack}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Visiting a Pack 662 meeting')}`}>
          Email the Cubmaster
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2>Signing up</h2>
      <p>
        Registration goes through Scouting America directly. This will take care of National & Council registration fees, then you will be officially registered with the pack. After that we will follow up with information on dues, uniforms, and the den your child will join.
      </p>
      {
        registrationReady ? (
          <p>
            <a class="cta" href={site.registrationUrl}>
              Register with Pack 662
            </a>
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p><Field value={site.registrationUrl} block /></p>
        )
      }
      <p class="meta">
        Still deciding? Our <a href={site.beAScoutUrl}>BeAScout unit page</a> has a
        Request More Information button, or just email us.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens after you register</h2>
      </div>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Pay pack dues.</strong> {site.cost.dues}, running from September.
          We invoice you through Scoutbook once your child is registered.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Get a uniform.</strong> From the{' '}
          <a href="/resources">Scout Shop</a>, or from our uniform exchange bins at a
          meeting, which is free and worth checking first.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fill out the health form.</strong> Parts A and B of the Annual Health
          and Medical Record, on the <a href="/resources">Resources</a> page. We do not
          need an insurance card, a doctor's signature or a vaccination record; just
          what is on the form.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Your child joins the den for their grade, and that den leader will be in touch
        with the den's schedule. Any adult who plans to volunteer also takes Scouting
        America's Safeguarding Youth training, which is free, online, and takes under an
        hour.
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Contact us if you have questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email.pack}`}>{site.email.pack}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
